# Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

All UI in KameOps must meet WCAG 2.1 AA. Apply these rules for every component and page.

## Semantic HTML

- Use `<button>` for actions, `<a>` for navigation, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<header>`, `<section>` where appropriate.
- Use heading order (h1 → h2 → h3) without skipping levels.
- Use `<Label htmlFor="id">` and associate every form control with an `id`.

## ARIA and labels

- Icon-only buttons: `aria-label="Descriptive action"` and `aria-hidden="true"` on the icon.
- Errors: `aria-describedby` pointing to error message `id`; error element can use `role="alert"`.
- Dialogs: use `aria-modal="true"` and focus trap (shadcn Dialog handles this).

## Keyboard and focus

- All interactive elements must be focusable and operable with keyboard (Tab, Enter, Space, arrows for lists/custom controls).
- Use visible focus styles in both themes: `focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring focus-visible:ring-offset-2`.
- Provide a “Skip to main content” link for keyboard users where appropriate.

## Contrast and theme

- Text contrast: at least 4.5:1 (normal text), 3:1 (large text). Use `text-foreground`, `text-muted-foreground`; avoid arbitrary low-contrast colors.
- Focus rings and borders must be visible in both light and dark mode.

## Checklist (before merging UI)

- [ ] Form fields have visible or programmatic labels
- [ ] Icon buttons have `aria-label`
- [ ] Focus order and focus visibility work in both themes
- [ ] No interactive element is keyboard-inaccessible
- [ ] Color is not the only way to convey information

For more patterns and testing, use the **accessibility** skill (`.cursor/skills/accessibility/`) and see `.cursor/rules/05-components.mdc` and `13-ui-ux-design.mdc`.
